Creating an Application in Salesforce.com Using Apex Programming 


1. Prerequisites
A Salesforce Developer Account
Sign up at: https://developer.salesforce.com/signup
Internet access and a modern web browser

2. Log in to Salesforce Developer Console
Open: https://login.salesforce.com
Log in using your Developer account
Click on the gear icon → Developer Console

3. Create a Custom Object (Part of the Application)
Go to Setup → Search for Objects → Click Object Manager
Click Create → Custom Object
Fill details:

Label: Student

Plural Label: Students

Object Name: Student

Enable options like "Allow Reports", "Track Field History", and click Save

Add custom fields (e.g., Name, Email, Course, Marks)

4. Create an Apex Class
In the Developer Console:
Click File → New → Apex Class
Name: StudentHandler
Paste the following code:
public class StudentHandler {
    
    // Method to insert a student record
    public static void createStudent(String name, String email, String course, Integer marks) {
        Student__c s = new Student__c();
        s.Name = name;
        s.Email__c = email;
        s.Course__c = course;
        s.Marks__c = marks;
        insert s;
    }

    // Method to fetch all students
    public static List<Student__c> getAllStudents() {
        return [SELECT Name, Email__c, Course__c, Marks__c FROM Student__c];
    }
}


5. Execute Apex Code (Anonymous Window)
In Developer Console → Debug → Open Execute Anonymous Window
Enter the following:

StudentHandler.createStudent('John Doe', 'john@example.com', 'Computer Engineering', 85);
Check the box Open Log, then click Execute

Check Debug Logs to verify execution

To view inserted data:
List<Student__c> students = StudentHandler.getAllStudents();
System.debug(students);

6. Verify in UI
Go to App Launcher → Search for Students
Click on it to view the inserted student records

